Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:27:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] analysis/melt_lens.jl: when the surface fresh layer is mixed
 down, and whether it follows the ice
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Daily over the first days (default 30), in the Beaufort Gyre, Central Arctic, Siberian shelves,
Archipelago and Baffin Bay: model − GLORYS salinity at the surface and over 15–40 m, ice speed and
under-ice u★ = √c_d |uᵢ − uₒ| (model and GLORYS, cells with > 15 % ice), the model's κᶜ at 10–40 m,
and model − GLORYS profiles of the top 60 m on days 1–30. Table melt_lens.md (with the correlation
of the daily growth of the surface excess with the u★³ excess) and figure melt_lens.png.

Why: the four-month NEMO run is too salty in the top ~10 m and too fresh at 15–40 m under ice from
September, with the full-depth freshwater content close to GLORYS: fresh water mixed down. The ice
is ~40 % too fast; this separates the ice's stirring from the ocean's own mixing.

